  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Arsenic Poisoning and the 4M&#x2019;s (Measure-Map-Manage-Mitigate) Pilot study to demonstrate the first rapid, digital, cloud-connected test to measure and map arsenic levels in Bangladesh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description akvo:type="5" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Excessive levels of arsenic in drinking water affect up to 50M people in Bangladesh, causing numerous health problems including cancer and killing tens-of-thousands each year. Current monitoring tools for onsite testing have serious drawbacks. AquAffirm has developed a new digital sensor/software system that will revolutionise arsenic management/mitigation, enabling real-time testing &amp; mapping, a development that could benefit millions. In this project the team will pilot the new technology and demonstrate its significant advantages, leading to increased awareness of this debilitating issue.</narrative>
  </description>
