    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fill in total number of current users for IWRM that are male and female

Fill the number of these users that are Domestic/School users, Public users

As this level has links with sanitation or drinking water. use the indicators D1 or S1 with their detailed descriptions to determine the service level</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2023"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="0"></target>
     <actual value="7700.00">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">07-04-2025: Out of the 700 wells tested, 77% were found to have contaminant levels exceeding established safety thresholds.  In response to these findings, we informed the users and owners of the affected wells and guided them to nearby alternatives with safe water. It is estimated that approximately 7,700 individuals rely on these wells, based on an average of 11 users per well. As these wells are located in communal areas, they are shared by residents living nearby.  Due to limitations in data collection, it was not possible to determine the gender distribution of the affected individuals; therefore, the total estimate has been evenly divided between males and females for reporting purposes.</narrative>
      </comment>
